# .dockerignore - files NOT sent to Docker as "build context" when building the service images.
# A smaller context makes `docker build` faster, and leaving out local build output and databases makes
# sure the image is built from source inside the container, not from whatever happens to be on the host.

# Host build output: the Dockerfile runs its own `dotnet publish`; copying host bin/obj could mix
# host-specific (e.g. Windows/macOS) artifacts into the Linux image.
**/bin/
**/obj/
# Local SQLite databases and their -shm/-wal files: an image must start with an empty, freshly seeded database.
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
# Git history: large and not needed to build.
.git/
# Runtime data folder.
data/
